From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Viewpoint bounds and navigation

Viewpoint.boundsMin/boundsMax and groundClearance (a physics ray down
to the solid below): mouse navigation and scripts slide along the
limits instead of leaving the world.

Left-drag orbits the surface the main view drew where it was pressed
(its depth buffer, the nearest within 4 px, so trees and impostors
count, which picking missed) when that surface is within 30 m (or 1.5x
the view's height above the ground) and within the bounds; over the sky
or farther scenery the view turns in place. Both turn 0.25 degree per
pixel the same way and stop 85 degrees from level. Pan and zoom drags
scale by the distance to the same surface; the wheel by the picked
object, else the solid a physics ray finds (2 m floor). Webots orbited
the picked point at 0.57 degree per pixel (land up to kilometres
away), turned in place 8x slower the other way, could flip over, and
scaled by the distance to the world origin when nothing was picked.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0012-viewpoint-bounds
- 0013-navigation-distance (its navigation part)
- 0071-navigation-orbit: camera travel for 200 px drags: valley from the
  high view 135 m -> 0 (turns in place), overview 97 -> 29-44 m, trunk
  34 -> 13 m; a 1000 px tilt flipped the view over -> stops at
  85 degrees
